{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3869","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3869","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3869\",\"parent_revision\":\"6f0c7824737c6dd06b46635d072f75b50e28e291\",\"root_revision\":\"9a8fd0483cae4ebe82bdd9e0bf05cac3fd2759e61dbde5cc56455b2da9ac1884\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-24\\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe local `brief~` identity cannot be safely created through the common provider boundary while create and update are indistinguishable. A collision can replace existing work rather than report that the reference is already owned.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User-confirmed Work Brief grilling session; 2026-09-24 provider-contract evidence\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-24\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Desired Outcome\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe provider-neutral backlog contract must separate creation from update. Generic `backlog add` accepts an optional `--reference`. A provider that supports caller-assigned references must honor it; a provider that cannot must create normally, return its canonical reference, and emit a warning. SQLite must support caller-assigned references. Creation is create-only: a collision is an error and must not overwrite, retry automatically, or become update through a force option. The collision response must identify the colliding reference and existing title, report `retryable: false`, direct same-work callers to update or groom the existing reference, and direct distinct-work callers to invoke creation again. Update and grooming must address an exact existing reference. A successful create response contains only the canonical `reference` and `warnings`; it does not duplicate acceptance state in another field.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe provider-neutral backlog contract must separate creation from update. Generic `backlog add` accepts an optional `--reference`. A provider that supports caller-assigned references must honor it; a provider that cannot must create normally, return its canonical reference, and emit a warning. SQLite must support caller-assigned references. Creation is create-only: a collision is an error and must not overwrite, retry automatically, or become update through a force option. The collision response must identify the colliding reference and existing title, report `retryable: false`, direct same-work callers to update or groom the existing reference, and direct distinct-work callers to invoke creation again. Update and grooming must address an exact existing reference. A successful create response contains only the canonical `reference` and `warnings`; it does not duplicate acceptance state in another field.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Gap And Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThe confirmed repository evidence shows an upsert-shaped `put_work_item` contract, with SQLite and memory providers able to overwrite an explicitly supplied reference. Generic creation does not expose the confirmed requested-reference behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThe confirmed repository evidence shows an upsert-shaped `put_work_item` contract, with SQLite and memory providers able to overwrite an explicitly supplied reference. Generic creation does not expose the confirmed requested-reference behavior.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Boundaries\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns provider-neutral create/update semantics and requested-reference behavior. It does not own `brief~` routing, add new lower-layer immutability machinery, define provider-specific identifiers, or add a `reference_accepted` field.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nThis Work Brief owns provider-neutral create/update semantics and requested-reference behavior. It does not own `brief~` routing, add new lower-layer immutability machinery, define provider-specific identifiers, or add a `reference_accepted` field.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Readiness And Acceptance Conditions\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nAn unused caller-assigned SQLite reference is created and returned canonically; recreating it fails without changing the existing item and returns the required non-retryable collision guidance. A provider that cannot honor a requested reference returns its own canonical reference with a warning. Updating or grooming an exact existing reference remains a distinct operation. All create outcomes use the minimal response contract.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nAn unused caller-assigned SQLite reference is created and returned canonically; recreating it fails without changing the existing item and returns the required non-retryable collision guidance. A provider that cannot honor a requested reference returns its own canonical reference with a warning. Updating or grooming an exact existing reference remains a distinct operation. All create outcomes use the minimal response contract.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ac792f2444ac327c9b41d137e385b9705bc581281f4c9125f46028cab2b1b98e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXCL7sg\"}"}